sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: fleet maintenance redesign (recipe.json read by Ansible, Tools phase last, recipe packages held). docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#converge-the-orbit-footprint.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: node:converge
  %% kind: node.converge
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant H as VPN hub<br/>WireGuard peers
  CLI->>GW: node:converge NODE
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:converge NODE`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> [--json]`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - brings one Node fully to the release: Orbit binaries, role software, roles, Tools and network
  %%> - every run applies all phases; each phase skips what already matches
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, lock Node, hub
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has an access grant to the target Node
  %%> - the target is an active, managed Linux Node (`node.converge_unsupported`)
  %%> - no other converge runs for the target or the hub; the Gateway holds one lock for each
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - targets only: the Node, its active roles, its Tools, its recorded network and the hub
  %%> - no versions: the playbooks read the pins of the release
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-converge
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task ID, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>SW: Write the playbook input<br/>inventory · vars · known_hosts
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the intent is too large for one environment value, so it goes to a private run file
  SW->>N: Install Orbit binaries<br/>Ansible phase: binaries
  %%> Why first:
  %%> - later phases and Doctor rely on the agent's facts and the `orbit-env` group
  %%> - it covers the agent's configuration and unit, the `orbit-env` access to Instance `.env` files, and the temporary-file cleanup rule; the agent restarts only when a file changed
  %%> - the Orbit CLI comes with it, so one converge brings a Node fully to the release
  SW->>N: Install role software<br/>Ansible phase: software
  %%> Why:
  %%> - installs the recipe's common and role tools at their pins, then holds them
  %%> - the hold keeps Tools from moving tested software; Ubuntu security updates still pass
  SW->>N: Configure the roles<br/>Ansible phase: roles
  %%> Best effort:
  %%> - closing world access on Instance `.env` files and clearing Route residue never fail the run; the next converge tries again
  opt Node has Tools
    SW->>N: Install Tools<br/>Ansible phase: tools
    %%> Why last of the software:
    %%> - a Tool that needs another version of a held package fails alone; role software stays as tested
    %%> On a Tool failure:
    %%> - the phase goes on with the other Tools and returns each Tool's result; only that Tool is marked failed
  end
  SW->>H: Apply the network<br/>Ansible phase: network
  %%> Why one phase on both Nodes:
  %%> - the peer and the hub change together; the hub first, then the Node, then a wait for the handshake
  %%> - no drift writes no file and reloads nothing
  SW->>N: Check the Node<br/>Ansible phase: check
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the one end check: role software, units, sites and a recent handshake
  %%> - a hub with no peers has no handshake to check, and a Node with no recorded hub skips the network phase
  alt check passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record converged state
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the task succeeds; a failed Tool is marked failed on its own record
  else a phase fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    Note over GW: Mark the task failed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the task fails with the failed phase
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - finished phases stay; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again: it starts from the first phase and skips what matches
  end
  opt run completed or failed
    SW->>SW: Remove the run folder<br/>private run files
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the intent, inventory and any secrets do not outlive the run, whatever its result
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
